    'missions.items.tmoment.name': 'T-Moment',
    'missions.items.tmoment.description': 'A digital experience designed around time, real-world use and the interactions that truly matter.',
    'missions.items.tmoment.category': 'Digital product',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.headerLabel': 'UNDO / AUDIO BUFFER',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.subtitle': 'Go back in time, just when you need to.',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.paragraph1': 'T-Moment starts with a simple but almost magical idea: what if we could go back a few moments and listen again to what just happened?',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.paragraph2': 'The application brings the idea of Undo into the real world. A conversation, something heard in passing, a sentence you want to hear again: T-Moment would let you rewind instantly and revisit that moment.',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.paragraph3': 'The first step focuses on audio. The application would temporarily retain what has just been heard so users could go back in time on demand, without having deliberately recorded the scene beforehand.',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.paragraph4': 'But the idea goes beyond simply rewinding audio. Eventually, the principle could extend to video, the browser or other digital environments: creating a kind of temporary memory that lets you return to what has just disappeared.',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.paragraph5': 'T-Moment is currently in development, with a launch planned for 2027. The ambition is to turn a gesture we all know from the digital world "Undo" into a new way of interacting with time.',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.timelineLabel': 'From the present moment back into the past',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.viewProject': 'View T-Moment',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.past': 'Past',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.now': 'Now',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.axis': 'Digital product',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.startLabel': 'Start',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.launchLabel': 'Target launch',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.principleLabel': 'Principle',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.principle': 'Listen → Go back → Listen again',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.firstFieldLabel': 'Initial medium',
    'missions.items.tmoment.transmission.firstField': 'Audio',
    'missions.items.audela.name': 'Au-delà',
    'missions.items.audela.description': 'A space for exploration beyond familiar formats, testing new interactions and imagining what might come next.',
    'missions.items.audela.category': 'Creative research',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.headerLabel': 'FORESIGHT / HORIZON',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.subtitle': 'What if our presence could transcend time?',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.paragraph1': 'Au-delà is probably the most ambitious idea to have emerged around NacoDev.',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.paragraph2': 'The project explores a question that is simple to formulate, yet immense in what it implies: how far can a human presence be extended into the digital world?',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.paragraph3': 'Today, we leave fragments of ourselves everywhere: words, a voice, images, choices, memories, habits, creations and ways of thinking. Au-delà imagines that one day, all these fragments might form something greater.',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.paragraph4': 'Not just an archive.',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.paragraph5': 'A digital presence capable of evolving, transmitting, telling stories and perhaps, one day, interacting.',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.paragraph6': 'The idea is not to predict exactly what technology will allow tomorrow. Au-delà is deliberately conceived as a horizon: a project able to evolve alongside advances in artificial intelligence, interfaces and the ways we preserve our data.',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.paragraph7': 'Some projects being developed today might one day become tiny building blocks of this vision.',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.paragraph8': 'Above all, Au-delà represents this conviction: the technologies we build now could profoundly change what it means to leave a trace of our passage.',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.timelineLabel': 'Trajectory towards the Au-delà horizon',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.viewProject': 'View Au-delà',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.axis': 'Research & future',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.status': 'Vision under exploration',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.horizonLabel': 'Horizon',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.horizon': 'Au-delà',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.principleLabel': 'Principle',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.principle': 'Preserve → Transmit → Extend',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.territoryLabel': 'Territory',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.territory': 'Identity · Memory · AI · Time',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.visionLabel': 'Vision',
    'missions.items.audela.transmission.vision': 'Digital continuity',
    'missions.items.web.name': 'Web experiments',
    'missions.items.web.description': 'Websites designed, built and launched to turn a real need into a useful, distinctive and lasting web experience.',
    'missions.items.web.category': 'Web design & development',
    'missions.items.web.period': '2021 → PRESENT',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.headerLabel': 'PROJECTS / ONLINE',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.subtitle': 'Concrete projects, real needs and solutions that truly exist.',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.paragraph1': 'Since 2021, NacoDev has also enabled me to turn very concrete requests into web experiences that people genuinely use.',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.paragraph2': 'Some projects began with a blank page and became complete websites. Others were more focused: unblocking a situation, improving an existing site, advising someone or helping them make the right technical choices.',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.paragraph3': 'I particularly enjoy these projects because they almost never begin with technology. They begin with a person, an activity, a problem or an idea that needs to become clearer.',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.paragraph4': 'Design, development, launch, recommendations or guidance: the format changes with the need.',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.paragraph5': 'These experiences reveal another side of NacoDev: building something useful and straightforward, then seeing it exist in the real world.',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.projectsLabel': 'Completed web projects',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.siteType': 'Website',
    'missions.items.web.transmission.online': 'Online',
